# SCRAMBLE -- the training canyon's theme, and the first music anyone hears
# in VECTRENCH.
#
# Originally written for VECTRENCH and imported from that project's score book:
# https://github.com/cfreder2/VECTRENCH  (src/songs.js)
#
# Written in the Mega Man 2 idiom rather than lifted from it: a driving sixteenth
# pulse, a bass that alternates root and octave instead of sitting on the beat,
# an arpeggio standing in for a chord the fourth voice cannot afford, and a fill
# that makes a section arrive rather than merely end.
#
# It is here because of what its ARRANGEMENT demonstrates. Nineteen order slots
# over nine written sections gives about two minutes from roughly seventy bars,
# and every section that lands twice in a row diverges on the second pass rather
# than repeating: A2 threads a countermelody under the hook's held tail, B2
# answers B's descent in parallel thirds, and C2 sequences the lift a third
# higher. No four bars repeat back to back unchanged.
#
# A minor throughout. A is the hook (i - bVI - bVII - V), B answers it a register
# up, C is the lift that keeps a two-minute arrangement from being one idea
# eleven times.

@track scramble
  name   SCRAMBLE
  bpm    150
  beats  16
  era    8bit
  tags   vectrench game original
  loop   1

